{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_grant_13.march","start_line":16,"start_col":9,"end_line":16,"end_col":13,"message":"`Cap(IO.FileWrite)` cannot be deserialized — a capability may only be received, never constructed, so `Handle` cannot derive Json.\nhint: hold the capability in a separate value and pass it as a parameter, keeping `Handle` free of capability fields.","code":"cap_deserialize","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_grant_13.march","start_line":18,"start_col":2,"end_line":20,"end_col":5,"message":"`main` performs IO but declares no grant. The program reaches `IO.Console`; a `main` with no capability parameter is granted nothing.\nhelp: declare the grant `main` actually needs —\n        fn main(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console)) : ()\nor grant everything with `fn main(cap : Cap(IO))`.\n`forge fix` can apply this.","code":"cap_grant","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":18,"start_col":9,"end_line":18,"end_col":11,"text":"(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console))"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
